      "rationale": "The tests exercise sqlparse.format(..., reindent_aligned=True), which uses AlignedIndentFilter (sqlparse/filters/aligned_indent.py). The expected alignment columns (6 = len('select') for FROM/WHERE/AND; 7 = len('select ') for continuation columns in an identifier list; 16 = len('select')+len('case ')+len('when ') for WHEN/ELSE/END in a CASE expression) are derived directly from the filter's own documented constants and formulas (``_max_kwd_len = len('select')``, the \"offset = 1 represent a single space after SELECT\" comment in ``nl()``, and the ``offset_ - len(str(stmt))`` computation in ``_process_case``), not from whatever the currently-buggy code happens to output. Because the reported regression breaks this alignment logic for exactly these three scenarios (basic, case statement, case statement with between), the tests fail on the current checkout and are expected to pass once the alignment bug is fixed, without constraining any other formatter behavior.",
